# W4-NEXT-2 K: row 18, selecting a built house. Builds one pioneer house (public (0,0), id 501,
# construction_full_proof.script's own proven-free tile 1156,516), selects it, screenshots the
# panel, deselects with Escape, builds a second house at a neighbouring tile, selects it, then
# demolishes it while selected - selection.hpp's own "a building demolished meanwhile drops the
# selection" exercised through the real window, not just the unit test.
resize 1024 768
wait frames 5
look 1140 516
key b
wait frames 5
click_px 833 330
wait frames 5
expect title build 501
click 1156 516
wait outcome
expect outcome Applied
checkpoint built_first

# Disarm the developer tool: while the menu is still open, a second B falls through to it
# (construction_handle's own key comment - the first B only opens the menu) and DevTool::handle's
# own Toggle flips `enabled_` false, since `arm()` had set it true (dev_tool.cpp). Cancel
# (the pickaxe/X click) does NOT clear this - selection needs the tool fully off
# (selection_active()'s own "!(dev_ enabled)"), not just the panel closed.
key b
wait frames 2
key esc
wait frames 5

# Select the first house: construction menu closed, the developer tool disarmed, a click on its
# tile falls to selection_handle.
click 1156 516
wait frames 5
expect title selected House
screenshot selected_house_live
checkpoint selected_first

# Escape deselects (K-1): the title drops "selected", the panel stops drawing.
key esc
wait frames 5
expect title-lacks selected
screenshot deselected_live
checkpoint deselected

# Build a second house clear of the first's 4x4 footprint (1156..1159), select it instead of the
# first (only one selection at a time).
key b
wait frames 5
click_px 833 330
wait frames 5
expect title build 501
click 1164 516
wait outcome
expect outcome Applied
checkpoint built_second
key b
wait frames 2
key esc
wait frames 5
click 1164 516
wait frames 5
expect title selected House
checkpoint selected_second

# Demolish the selected building while it is selected: the menu reopens on the grid (not the
# panel), but dev_ is still disarmed from the "key b" above, so one more B (now that the menu is
# open) re-enables it (DevTool::handle's own Toggle) before the pickaxe's click can reach
# ToggleDemolish at all (DevTool::handle returns early while `!enabled_`).
key b
wait frames 2
key b
wait frames 2
click_px 996 736
wait frames 2
click 1164 516
wait outcome
expect outcome Applied
expect title-lacks selected
checkpoint demolished_while_selected

key esc
wait frames 5
quit
